{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JPJ59RwsCkx1AekGZ3WhfG","type":"tool_result","content":"120\t    SECRETS-only (PLAN-158 Wave 2, spec-conformance): the E1 §4 gate is scoped\n121\t    to LIVE CREDENTIALS by its own docstring, but scan()'s ALL_PATTERNS default\n122\t    also swept the 11 LGPD/BR PII families — checksum-valid numeric collisions\n123\t    (a benign GitHub run id that happens to pass the CPF checksum; `br_rg`\n124\t    matching ANY bare 8-9 digit run) fail-CLOSED blocked benign commands with\n125\t    no env escape (S270 live incident). Restrict THIS pre-exec scan to the\n126\t    token/credential families; the PII families stay in the shared catalog and\n127\t    keep being consumed by the egress-redaction rail, where PII belongs.\n128\t    Degradation is fail-CLOSED-preserving: if SECRETS is unavailable\n129\t    (older _lib), fall back to the full catalog (over-block, never under-block).\n130\t    \"\"\"\n131\t    if _secret_patterns is None or not command:\n132\t        return False\n133\t    try:\n134\t        families = getattr(_secret_patterns, \"SECRETS\", None)\n135\t        return bool(_secret_patterns.scan(command, patterns=families))\n136\t    except Exception:  # pragma: no cover — fail-OPEN\n137\t        return False\n138\t\n139\t\n140\tdef _evaluate(command: str) -> Tuple[Optional[str], Optional[str], Optional[str]]:\n141\t    \"\"\"Return (decision, rule_id, rule_class) or (None, None, None).\n142\t\n143\t    decision ∈ {deny, ask, advisory}. Secret-in-command short-circuits to a\n144\t    secret-class hit BEFORE the .md rules (highest-credential surface). Pure-ish"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99e4484c-9fd2-48bc-96cb-ca1217c6fa39","uuid":"c4ecb2ae-dbd4-4e85-ac73-eb91afa4a0a0","timestamp":"2026-11-15T10:37:11.012Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.tG8bbW/tree/.claude/hooks/check_adversary.py","content":"    SECRETS-only (PLAN-158 Wave 2, spec-conformance): the E1 §4 gate is scoped\n    to LIVE CREDENTIALS by its own docstring, but scan()'s ALL_PATTERNS default\n    also swept the 11 LGPD/BR PII families — checksum-valid numeric collisions\n    (a benign GitHub run id that happens to pass the CPF checksum; `br_rg`\n    matching ANY bare 8-9 digit run) fail-CLOSED blocked benign commands with\n    no env escape (S270 live incident). Restrict THIS pre-exec scan to the\n    token/credential families; the PII families stay in the shared catalog and\n    keep being consumed by the egress-redaction rail, where PII belongs.\n    Degradation is fail-CLOSED-preserving: if SECRETS is unavailable\n    (older _lib), fall back to the full catalog (over-block, never under-block).\n    \"\"\"\n    if _secret_patterns is None or not command:\n        return False\n    try:\n        families = getattr(_secret_patterns, \"SECRETS\", None)\n        return bool(_secret_patterns.scan(command, patterns=families))\n    except Exception:  # pragma: no cover — fail-OPEN\n        return False\n\n\ndef _evaluate(command: str) -> Tuple[Optional[str], Optional[str], Optional[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Return (decision, rule_id, rule_class) or (None, None, None).\n\n    decision ∈ {deny, ask, advisory}. Secret-in-command short-circuits to a\n    secret-class hit BEFORE the .md rules (highest-credential surface). Pure-ish","numLines":25,"startLine":120,"totalLines":286}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JPJ59RwsCkx1AekGZ3WhfG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
